// D-PERSIST1 — `@Persist` dev-hot-reload state survival.
// A module-level binding marked `@Persist` is meant to survive a `jet dev`
// hot reload instead of resetting (identity = module path + binding name).
// Release semantics are identical with or without the marker — this example
// documents the surface and its ordinary (non-dev) run: `@Persist` is inert
// here, so `counter` is simply its initial value.
//
// The dev-reload carry-across itself needs a module-plus-name-keyed value
// store in the JIT resident runtime (`crates/jet-jit`), which doesn't exist
// yet — see the D-PERSIST1 row in docs/spec/syntax-decisions.md for the
// named gate. This example is golden-tested for the ordinary run only.

@Persist const counter = 0

fn main() {
    print("{counter}")
}
// --- expected output --------------------------------------------------
// 0
